# persianPerch: scentTrail, perch's own SQLite (events, states, litters, rollups, vitals).
# It runs in WAL mode, so the live file must never be copied as a file (no path line); the
# sqlite line takes a consistent .dump instead (stacks/README.md -> backup). Everything else
# perch holds is rebuilt from the fleet within minutes of a restart, so this is the whole
# data backup. The settings (secrets.env.local) are backed up by backup.sh with every node's
# other settings. `optional`: the database only exists once perch has started.
sqlite  persian-perch  persian-perch/scentTrail.db  optional
